00:11:50.543 --> 00:11:51.510
I like Red Bull.

00:11:51.510 --> 00:11:53.913
Sugar-free is exactly the same thing.

00:11:53.913 --> 00:11:55.247
This one had less of an aftertaste,

00:11:55.247 --> 00:11:56.749
which actually, I didn't really like.

00:11:56.749 --> 00:11:58.284
Coconut and dragon fruit.

00:11:59.351 --> 00:12:02.221
Suntan lotion and pee.

00:12:02.221 --> 00:12:04.190
Watermelon, I liked.

00:12:04.190 --> 00:12:06.092
Blue, a little too tart.

00:12:06.092 --> 00:12:08.694
Peach, I enjoyed.

00:12:08.694 --> 00:12:10.229
Fig apple, trash.

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:13.365
And tropical, not bad.

00:12:13.365 --> 00:12:16.302
My main takeaways from that,
firstly, I need to lie down.

00:12:16.302 --> 00:12:17.670
If we can make that happen,
that would be great.

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:20.005
Secondly, I think the sugar-free
versions are overwhelmingly

00:12:20.005 --> 00:12:22.675
worse-tasting than the sugar versions are.

00:12:22.675 --> 00:12:23.743
I also think for me, like I say,

00:12:23.743 --> 00:12:26.245
I don't love the taste
of just normal Red Bull,

00:12:26.245 --> 00:12:28.080
so I think I've ended up liking the ones

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:29.749
which are flavored with
things which aren't Red Bull.

00:12:29.749 --> 00:12:30.916
So that makes sense.

00:12:33.452 --> 00:12:34.320
What about the price?

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:36.589
Well, in the UK, a 250-milliliter can

00:12:36.589 --> 00:12:39.225
will cost you 1.50 pounds
at a Tesco supermarket.

00:12:39.225 --> 00:12:42.094
That works out to roughly 60
pence per 100 milliliters,

00:12:42.094 --> 00:12:44.029
which is around 74 cents.

00:12:44.029 --> 00:12:44.864
In the US,

00:12:44.864 --> 00:12:48.367
The cost of this
250-milliliter Red Bull can

00:12:48.367 --> 00:12:50.803
at Walmart is $2.18,

00:12:50.803 --> 00:12:53.939
which breaks it down to 80
cents per 100 milliliters.

00:12:53.939 --> 00:12:54.807
So it looks like the UK

00:12:54.807 --> 00:12:56.208
is actually getting a slightly better deal

00:12:56.208 --> 00:12:57.476
on its Red Bull than the US is.

00:12:57.476 --> 00:12:58.644
That's actually kind of a Food Wars first,

00:12:58.644 --> 00:13:00.012
so it doesn't happen often.

00:13:02.381 --> 00:13:03.616
In the UK, our standard Red Bull

00:13:03.616 --> 00:13:05.551
contains the following ingredients:

00:13:05.551 --> 00:13:09.488
water, sucrose, glucose,
acidifier citric acid,

00:13:09.488 --> 00:13:11.257
taurine, sodium carbonates

00:13:11.257 --> 00:13:15.628
and magnesium carbonate, caffeine,
niacin, pantothenic acid,

00:13:15.628 --> 00:13:19.231
vitamin B6, vitamin
B12 flavorings, colors,

00:13:19.231 --> 00:13:21.767
caramel and riboflavin,
and carbon dioxide.

00:13:21.767 --> 00:13:23.969
Our Red Bull in the US
contains pretty much

00:13:23.969 --> 00:13:24.870
the same stuff.

00:13:24.870 --> 00:13:29.742
Carbonated water, sucrose,
glucose, citric acid, taurine,

00:13:29.742 --> 00:13:33.646
sodium bicarbonate, magnesium
carbonate, caffeine.

00:13:35.047 --> 00:13:36.816
Niacinamide.

00:13:36.816 --> 00:13:41.687
Calcium pantothenate.

00:13:41.687 --> 00:13:45.024
Pyridoxine HCI.

00:13:45.024 --> 00:13:47.059
Vitamin B12, natural
and artificial flavors.

00:13:47.059 --> 00:13:47.893
All right.

00:13:47.893 --> 00:13:50.229
The vitamins have different
names, but it's all the same.

00:13:50.229 --> 00:13:52.231
You may notice the ingredient
taurine on that list.

00:13:52.231 --> 00:13:53.599
Now, taurine has been the subject of

00:13:53.599 --> 00:13:56.035
inaccurate rumors on
the internet for years.

00:13:56.035 --> 00:13:57.736
Taurine has an association with bulls,

00:13:57.736 --> 00:14:00.172
drawing its name from the
Latin word for bull, taurus.

00:14:00.172 --> 00:14:01.240
Some people run with this

00:14:01.240 --> 00:14:04.076
and falsely claim that
it's code for bull semen.

00:14:04.076 --> 00:14:05.611
The name actually comes from the fact that

00:14:05.611 --> 00:14:08.280
taurine was first isolated from ox bile.

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:12.184
OK, the good news is that
there's no ox spit in Red Bull,

00:14:12.184 --> 00:14:15.120
as food producers have used a
synthetic version of taurine

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:17.656
that isn't derived from animals.

00:14:17.656 --> 00:14:20.025
It also means that Red Bull
is suitable for vegans.

00:14:20.025 --> 00:14:22.728
One study found that exposing
human teeth to energy drinks

00:14:22.728 --> 00:14:24.630
for 15 minutes, four times a day,

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:26.065
resulted in a significant

00:14:26.065 --> 00:14:28.167
and irreversible loss of tooth enamel.

00:14:28.167 --> 00:14:29.201
The study also noted that

00:14:29.201 --> 00:14:31.770
energy drinks were twice as
harmful as regular soft drinks

00:14:31.770 --> 00:14:32.605
to tooth enamel.

00:14:32.605 --> 00:14:33.939
As the study in rats found,

00:14:33.939 --> 00:14:36.542
chronic intake of Red
Bull may cause a decline

00:14:36.542 --> 00:14:37.743
in kidney function.

00:14:37.743 --> 00:14:39.945
However, these results
have not been replicated

00:14:39.945 --> 00:14:41.213
in human studies.

00:14:41.213 --> 00:14:44.283
But any excuse to see my
boys, the dancing rats.

00:14:48.721 --> 00:14:51.090
Red Bull in the UK contains 110 calories

00:14:51.090 --> 00:14:53.192
per 250-milliliter can.

00:14:53.192 --> 00:14:55.961
One of these cans also
contains 27 grams of sugar.

00:14:55.961 --> 00:14:56.929
According to their website,

00:14:56.929 --> 00:14:58.330
this is actually a similar amount of sugar

00:14:58.330 --> 00:15:00.633
to what you might find
in say, apple juice.

00:15:00.633 --> 00:15:02.668
Both sugar-free Red Bull and Red Bull Zero

00:15:02.668 --> 00:15:06.805
contain 10 calories per
this 8.4-fluid-ounce can.

00:15:06.805 --> 00:15:10.509
Sugar-free replace their sugar with

00:15:11.710 --> 00:15:15.381
acesulfame potassium and aspartame.

00:15:15.381 --> 00:15:17.383
Red Bull Zero replaced sugar with

00:15:18.284 --> 00:15:21.754
acesulfame potassium K and sucralose.

00:15:21.754 --> 00:15:23.589
Acesulfame potassium, or Ace K,

00:15:23.589 --> 00:15:25.557
which is Red Bull's
zero-calorie sweetener,

00:15:25.557 --> 00:15:27.693
has had its share of
controversy over the years.

00:15:27.693 --> 00:15:28.494
Although, to be fair,

00:15:28.494 --> 00:15:31.397
a lot of the studies this came
from were done in the 1970s.

00:15:31.397 --> 00:15:33.532
This has led to the validity
being called into question

00:15:33.532 --> 00:15:34.466
in recent years.

00:15:34.466 --> 00:15:36.235
According to Healthline.com,

00:15:36.235 --> 00:15:38.904
in 1996, the Center for
Science in the Public Interest

00:15:38.904 --> 00:15:41.307
urged the FDA to do more testing on Ace K

00:15:41.307 --> 00:15:43.275
before allowing its
inclusion in soft drinks.

00:15:43.275 --> 00:15:46.378
The CSPI go on to say that there are

00:15:46.378 --> 00:15:48.480
health concerns associated with a Ace K,

00:15:48.480 --> 00:15:50.816
including cancer, hormone disruption,

00:15:50.816 --> 00:15:53.252
and risks to pregnant people.

00:15:53.252 --> 00:15:54.787
There's also a study that determined

00:15:54.787 --> 00:15:57.156
the chronic use of Ace K in male mice

00:15:57.156 --> 00:15:59.625
was linked to possible
changes in brain function

00:15:59.625 --> 00:16:01.060
over a period of 40 weeks.

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:02.761
Yeah, I believe that it's been 40 minutes,

00:16:02.761 --> 00:16:05.464
and my brain is just.

00:16:05.464 --> 00:16:07.299
One of the perceived
benefits of drinking Red Bull

00:16:07.299 --> 00:16:09.001
is that it's supposed
to give people a boost

00:16:09.001 --> 00:16:10.035
through its caffeine content.

00:16:10.035 --> 00:16:13.472
A 250-milliliter can contains
80 milligrams of caffeine.

00:16:13.472 --> 00:16:14.373
But is that a lot?

00:16:14.373 --> 00:16:15.708
Compared to other soft drinks?

00:16:15.708 --> 00:16:16.542
Yeah.

00:16:16.542 --> 00:16:19.812
A 12-ounce can of Coke contains
34 milligrams of caffeine.

00:16:19.812 --> 00:16:21.747
That's less than half
the amount of caffeine

00:16:21.747 --> 00:16:24.149
and almost double the amount
of fluid as this Red Bull.

00:16:24.149 --> 00:16:25.384
A 12-ounce can of Mountain Dew

00:16:25.384 --> 00:16:28.387
contains slightly more,
with 55 milligrams.

00:16:28.387 --> 00:16:30.923
If we compare Red Bull to
another popular energy drink,

00:16:30.923 --> 00:16:34.526
Monster, you'll find that
they actually have the same

00:16:34.526 --> 00:16:36.462
caffeine content per 100 milliliters,

00:16:36.462 --> 00:16:38.097
which is 32 milligrams.

00:16:38.097 --> 00:16:39.365
Although Monster cans tend to be bigger,

00:16:39.365 --> 00:16:41.166
so you are getting more caffeine in total.

00:16:41.166 --> 00:16:42.301
The caffeine amount, however,

00:16:42.301 --> 00:16:45.504
can be a bit underwhelming when
compared to regular coffee.

00:16:45.504 --> 00:16:48.207
An eight-ounce, 237-milligram

00:16:48.207 --> 00:16:52.578
brewed coffee contains on average
95 milligrams of caffeine,

00:16:52.578 --> 00:16:56.315
and a double shot of espresso
contains 125 milligrams.

00:16:56.315 --> 00:16:57.349
One issue comes from the fact that

00:16:57.349 --> 00:16:59.585
some people will consider Red
Bull to be more like a soda,

00:16:59.585 --> 00:17:01.353
and therefore might drink
higher quantities of it.

00:17:01.353 --> 00:17:03.322
So is it possible to overdose on Red Bull?

00:17:03.322 --> 00:17:05.891
Yeah, although highly unlikely.

00:17:05.891 --> 00:17:08.427
Caffeine-related deaths have
been found in individuals

00:17:08.427 --> 00:17:11.230
that intake somewhere
between 3 and 5 grams —

00:17:11.230 --> 00:17:14.500
not milligrams, grams —
of caffeine in one day.

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:16.368
That would be 40 of these.

00:17:16.368 --> 00:17:18.804
I feel like your bladder
would explode first.

00:17:18.804 --> 00:17:20.305
Although apparently, that
wasn't enough caffeine

00:17:20.305 --> 00:17:21.173
for some people.

00:17:21.173 --> 00:17:24.109
In 2014, Red Bull was sued
in a class-action lawsuit

00:17:24.109 --> 00:17:25.477
around false advertising.

00:17:25.477 --> 00:17:27.780
Remember the ad campaign
"Red Bull gives you wings"?

00:17:27.780 --> 00:17:28.947
Well, it doesn't.

00:17:28.947 --> 00:17:30.049
False advertising.

00:17:30.049 --> 00:17:32.918
Back then, Red Bull did
say in its marketing

00:17:32.918 --> 00:17:34.987
that this drink could
improve concentration

00:17:34.987 --> 00:17:36.388
and reaction speeds,

00:17:36.388 --> 00:17:38.690
a claim that lacked
any scientific support.

00:17:38.690 --> 00:17:40.259
Furthermore, the suit said that Red Bull

00:17:40.259 --> 00:17:42.461
persistently and pervasively
market their product

00:17:42.461 --> 00:17:45.597
as a superior source of energy,
worthy of a premium price

00:17:45.597 --> 00:17:48.367
over a cup of coffee or
other sources of caffeine.

00:17:48.367 --> 00:17:51.804
Red Bull did agree to a
$13 million settlement,

00:17:51.804 --> 00:17:53.939
which granted anyone
who purchased a Red Bull

00:17:53.939 --> 00:17:56.542
dating back the January 1, 2002,

00:17:56.542 --> 00:18:00.345
was entitled to $10 or
$15 worth of Red Bull.

00:18:03.248 --> 00:18:06.785
It looks and sounds exactly like pee.

00:18:09.154 --> 00:18:11.857
Ugh. Good morning.

